{"parentUuid":"9ae7854f-7a02-4eaa-add1-f173c3bc76af","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ac68b9dc-9847-4e6f-8ec2-6b4367414408","agentId":"a2d29f537e2b0ba30","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018P1gghNBKiQ4LNUES1CMRR","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Cross-Entropy Method CEM Rubinstein combinatorial optimization 2024 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"The Cross-Entropy Method: A Unified Approach to Combinatorial Optimization, Monte-Carlo Simulation and Machine Learning | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-1-4757-4321-0\"},{\"title\":\"Amazon.com: The Cross-Entropy Method: A Unified Approach to Combinatorial Optimization, Monte-Carlo Simulation and Machine Learning (Information Science and Statistics): 9780387212401: Rubinstein, Reuven Y., Kroese, Dirk P.: Books\",\"url\":\"https://www.amazon.com/Cross-Entropy-Method-Combinatorial-Optimization-Monte-Carlo/dp/038721240X\"},{\"title\":\"The cross-entropy method : a unified approach to combinatorial optimization, Monte-Carlo simulation, and machine learning : Rubenstein, Reuven Y : Free Download, Borrow, and Streaming : Internet Archive\",\"url\":\"https://archive.org/details/springer_10.1007-978-1-4757-4321-0\"},{\"title\":\"The Cross-Entropy Method: A Unified Approach to Combinatorial Optimization ... - Reuven Y. Rubinstein, Dirk P. Kroese - Google Books\",\"url\":\"https://books.google.com/books/about/The_Cross_Entropy_Method.html?id=9KZCZIogU4YC\"},{\"title\":\"A Tutorial on the Cross-Entropy Method Pieter-Tjerk de Boer\",\"url\":\"https://web.mit.edu/6.454/www/www_fall_2003/gew/CEtutorial.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"The Cross-Entropy Method for Combinatorial and Continuous Optimization | Methodology and Computing in Applied Probability | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1023/A:1010091220143\"},{\"title\":\"Cross-entropy method - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cross-entropy_method\"},{\"title\":\"Amazon.com: The Cross-Entropy Method: A Unified Approach to Combinatorial Optimization, Monte-Carlo Simulation and Machine Learning: 9781475743227: Rubinstein, Reuven Y., Kroese, Dirk P.: Books\",\"url\":\"https://www.amazon.com/Cross-Entropy-Method-Combinatorial-Optimization-Monte-Carlo/dp/147574322X\"},{\"title\":\"The Cross-Entropy Method: A Unified Approach to Combinatorial Optimization, Monte-Carlo Simulation and Machine Learning (Information Science and Statistics) - Rubinstein, Reuven Y.; Kroese, Dirk P.: 9780387212401 - AbeBooks\",\"url\":\"https://www.abebooks.com/9780387212401/Cross-Entropy-Method-Unified-Approach-Combinatorial-038721240X/plp\"},{\"title\":\"The Cross-Entropy Method: A Unified Approach to Combinatorial Optimization, Monte-Carlo Simulation and Machine Learning / Edition 1 by Reuven Y. Rubinstein, Dirk P. Kroese | | 9781441919403 | Paperback | Barnes & Noble®\",\"url\":\"https://www.barnesandnoble.com/w/cross-entropy-method-reuven-y-rubinstein/1101668516\"}]\n\nI've completed the web search for your query about the Cross-Entropy Method (CEM), Rubinstein, and combinatorial optimization. Here's what I found:\n\n## Key Findings:\n\n**About the Cross-Entropy Method:**\n\nThe cross-entropy (CE) method is a Monte Carlo method for importance sampling and optimization that is applicable to both combinatorial and continuous problems, with either a static or noisy objective.\n\n**Historical Development:**\n\nThe CE method started around 1997 when Rubinstein proposed an adaptive algorithm for rare-event simulation using cross-entropy minimization, and it was soon realized that the underlying ideas could be adapted to tackle general combinatorial and multi-extremal optimization problems.\n\n**Rubinstein's Role:**\n\nRubinstein is the pioneer of the well-known score-function and cross-entropy methods. Rubinstein developed the method in the context of rare-event simulation, and the method has been applied to the traveling salesman, quadratic assignment, DNA sequence alignment, max-cut and buffer allocation problems.\n\n**Primary Reference:**\n\nThe seminal work is \"The Cross-Entropy Method: A Unified Approach to Combinatorial Optimization, Monte-Carlo Simulation and Machine Learning\" by Rubinstein and Kroese, which serves as the comprehensive reference for the field.\n\nThe search results did not contain recent publications from 2024-2025 specifically, but the foundational concepts and applications of CEM remain well-established in the literature.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"ffcefe43-d652-4d49-aaa2-68b13a54dfd1","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:10:26.570Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9ae7854f-7a02-4eaa-add1-f173c3bc76af","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"f875ce8d-c06a-4961-8806-34132fb5fcca","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ac68b9dc-9847-4e6f-8ec2-6b4367414408","agentId":"a2d29f537e2b0ba30","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UzzUuwr62n2qD6wgY4hU4k","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"MCMC combinatorial optimization 2025 sampling SAT placement\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"SAT-sampling for statistical significance testing in sparse contingency tables\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2511.05709\"},{\"title\":\"Quantum-classical Algorithms Advance Combinatorial Optimization With Fair Ground-State Sampling\",\"url\":\"https://quantumzeitgeist.com/quantum-optimization-classical-algorithms-advance-combinatorial-fair-ground-state-sampling/\"},{\"title\":\"Near-Uniform Sampling of Combinatorial Spaces Using XOR Constraints\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.cornell.edu/~sabhar/publications/xorSamplingNIPS06.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"MCMC Sampling - Stan\",\"url\":\"https://mc-stan.org/docs/reference-manual/mcmc.html\"},{\"title\":\"Revisiting Sampling for Combinatorial Optimization | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/forum?id=ZMP0Bki9aK\"},{\"title\":\"Latent Guided Sampling for Combinatorial Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2506.03672\"},{\"title\":\"Fast Sampling and Counting k-SAT Solutions in the Local Lemma Regime | Journal of the ACM\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3469832\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - Thinklab-SJTU/awesome-ml4co: Awesome machine learning for combinatorial optimization papers. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/Thinklab-SJTU/awesome-ml4co\"},{\"title\":\"Revisiting Sampling for Combinatorial Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://proceedings.mlr.press/v202/sun23c.html\"},{\"title\":\"C H A P T E R 12 THE MARKOV CHAIN MONTE CARLO METHOD: AN APPROACH\",\"url\":\"https://people.eecs.berkeley.edu/~sinclair/mcmc.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here are the key findings related to MCMC, combinatorial optimization, sampling, and SAT:\n\n## SAT-Based Sampling and MCMC\n\nA recent approach encodes fibers as Boolean circuits to allow modern SAT samplers to generate tables randomly, with analysis of sampling bias and practical mitigation strategies. Hybrid MCMC schemes combine SAT proposals with local moves to ensure correct stationary distributions, which is particularly beneficial in presence of structural zeros.\n\n## Quantum-Classical MCMC for SAT Problems\n\nResearchers have developed hybrid quantum-classical Markov chain Monte Carlo algorithms that combine quantum dynamics with classical acceptance steps to correct biases and restore near-uniform sampling. For random 2-SAT instances, hybrid MCMC combining quantum-assisted neural proposals with single spin-flip updates achieves fairness comparable to established algorithms, while for random 3-SAT problems, the method maintains approximately uniform sampling.\n\n## Revival of Sampling for Combinatorial Optimization\n\nRecent work has revisited sampling for combinatorial optimization, motivated by advances in gradient-based discrete MCMC and parallel neighborhood exploration techniques, finding that modern sampling strategies can provide general-purpose solvers that are competitive with state-of-the-art combinatorial solvers.\n\n## Markov Chain Approaches for SAT Counting\n\nNew algorithms based on Markov chains sample and approximately count satisfying assignments to k-uniform CNF formulas, using the local lemma to bypass the connectivity barrier in traditional MCMC approaches on disconnected state spaces like SAT solutions.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"acaaf236-c2e7-4fc4-bc9a-5ec8d4e0b3c7","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:10:27.182Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f875ce8d-c06a-4961-8806-34132fb5fcca","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"2b030181-c839-4c59-b664-024dd52b2ec8","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ac68b9dc-9847-4e6f-8ec2-6b4367414408","agentId":"a2d29f537e2b0ba30","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xq8TJQRsHXi8zxJ23fV5qq","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Sequential Monte Carlo SMC combinatorial optimization 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Sequential Monte Carlo optimization and statistical inference - Duan - 2023 - WIREs Computational Statistics - Wiley Online Library\",\"url\":\"https://wires.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/wics.1598\"},{\"title\":\"On-line optimization of sequential Monte Carlo methods using stochastic approximation | IEEE Conference Publication | IEEE Xplore\",\"url\":\"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/1025171/\"},{\"title\":\"[2505.16732] Sequential Monte Carlo for Policy Optimization in Continuous POMDPs\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.16732\"},{\"title\":\"Sequential Monte Carlo Algorithms\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/sequential-monte-carlo-algorithm\"},{\"title\":\"Scalable sequential Monte Carlo methods and probabilistic approach to combinatorial problems - UBC Library Open Collections\",\"url\":\"https://open.library.ubc.ca/soa/cIRcle/collections/ubctheses/24/items/1.0362870\"},{\"title\":\"[Literature Review] Sequential Monte Carlo for Policy Optimization in Continuous POMDPs\",\"url\":\"https://www.themoonlight.io/en/review/sequential-monte-carlo-for-policy-optimization-in-continuous-pomdps\"},{\"title\":\"Sequential Monte Carlo Simulated Annealing Enlu Zhou Xi Chen\",\"url\":\"https://enluzhou.gatech.edu/papers/SMCSA_Aug05.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Repetition effects in a Sequential Monte Carlo sampler\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2409.19017\"},{\"title\":\"Amazon.com: Fast Sequential Monte Carlo Methods for Counting and Optimization (Wiley Series in Probability and Statistics): 9781118612262: Rubinstein, Reuven Y., Ridder, Ad, Vaisman, Radislav: Books\",\"url\":\"https://www.amazon.com/Sequential-Counting-Optimization-Probability-Statistics/dp/1118612264\"},{\"title\":\"[2402.07963] SPO: Sequential Monte Carlo Policy Optimisation\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2402.07963\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Sequential Monte Carlo (SMC) and combinatorial optimization:\n\n## Key Applications and Techniques\n\nAll optimization tasks (continuous, discontinuous, combinatorial, or noisy objective function) can be turned into sampling problems where SMC can be applied. Density-tempered SMC is a highly efficient sampling technique ideally suited for challenging global optimization problems.\n\n## SMC Approach to Combinatorial Optimization\n\nThe SMC approach to combinatorial optimization invented by Duan (2019) is a provable approach relying on Monte Carlo convergence that is not meta-heuristic because convergence to the right solution is ensured as the sample size gets large. The methodological essence of SMC optimization for combinatorial problems is to view the optimization target as a discrete probability function and proceed to sample from it, with the point yielding the highest probability being the SMC solution and the method obtaining the global maximum with a sufficiently large particle set.\n\n## Recent 2025 Research\n\nA nested sequential Monte Carlo (SMC) algorithm has been developed that efficiently estimates a history-dependent policy gradient under samples from the optimal trajectory distribution induced by POMDPs. Additionally, SPO (Sequential Monte Carlo Policy Optimisation) is a model-based reinforcement learning algorithm grounded within the Expectation Maximisation (EM) framework.\n\n## General Advantages\n\nSampling methods have several advantages over traditional optimization methods, being generic and in principle applicable to all optimization problems, with Monte Carlo simulation being good for high-dimensional problems because the convergence rate is typically invariant to the dimension, and being derivative-free.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"12411fea-9eee-4d69-9074-1fb1ac99b9b5","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:10:27.831Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2b030181-c839-4c59-b664-024dd52b2ec8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"9c119089-0446-47e1-9b33-c7edffb9a4f1","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ac68b9dc-9847-4e6f-8ec2-6b4367414408","agentId":"a2d29f537e2b0ba30","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015Ew5GMaQAL4rT5RzPEEh77","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"parallel tempering replica exchange combinatorial optimization 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Parallel tempering - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parallel_tempering\"},{\"title\":\"A Permutational Boltzmann Machine with Parallel Tempering for Solving Combinatorial Optimization Problems | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-58112-1_22\"},{\"title\":\"IsingFormer: Augmenting Parallel Tempering With Learned Proposals\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2509.23043v1\"},{\"title\":\"[2509.23043] IsingFormer: Augmenting Parallel Tempering With Learned Proposals\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.23043\"},{\"title\":\"IsingFormer: Augmenting Parallel Tempering with Learned Proposals | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/forum?id=yQuTa0yukr\"},{\"title\":\"Two-dimensional Parallel Tempering for Constrained Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2506.14781v2\"},{\"title\":\"Design of proteins by parallel tempering in the sequence space - PubMed\",\"url\":\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40990840/\"},{\"title\":\"Generalised Parallel Tempering: Flexible Replica Exchange via Flows and Diffusions\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2502.10328v1\"},{\"title\":\"Decentralized Replica Exchange Parallel Tempering: An Efficient Implementation of Parallel Tempering Using MPI and SPRNG | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-540-74484-9_44\"},{\"title\":\"Parallel tempering–inspired distributed binary optimization with in-memory computing | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/389872012_Parallel_tempering-inspired_distributed_binary_optimization_with_in-memory_computing\"}]\n\nI've completed the web search on \"parallel tempering replica exchange combinatorial optimization 2025\". Here are the key findings:\n\n## Overview\n\nParallel tempering (also known as replica exchange MCMC sampling), is a simulation method aimed at improving the dynamic properties of Monte Carlo method simulations of physical systems, and of Markov chain Monte Carlo (MCMC) sampling methods more generally.\n\n## Recent 2025 Developments\n\nSeveral notable 2025 advancements have emerged:\n\n**IsingFormer (September 2025):** A Transformer trained on equilibrium samples that can generate entire spin configurations resembling those from the target distribution. These uncorrelated samples are used as proposals for global moves within a Metropolis step in PT, complementing the usual single-spin flips. On 3D spin glasses (optimization), PT enhanced with IsingFormer finds substantially lower-energy states, demonstrating how global moves accelerate search in rugged landscapes.\n\n**Two-Dimensional Parallel Tempering (2D-PT):** A method that extends PT to a second dimension with multiple energy landscapes to accelerate sampling under constraints.\n\n**Generalized Parallel Tempering (February 2025):** A mathematically formalized framework that combines the benefits of neural samplers with the robustness of PT, termed Generalised Parallel Tempering (GePT).\n\n**Protein Design Applications (2025):** Parallel tempering is shown to be a viable alternative to Monte Carlo sampling without replica exchanges and simulated annealing or related energy-based protein design methods.\n\n## Combinatorial Optimization Applications\n\nA Permutational Boltzmann Machine with Parallel Tempering is capable of solving NP-Hard problems such as QAP in excess of 100× faster than other state-of-the-art solvers.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"a25f70eb-2149-4177-a3fb-53622db337f8","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:10:29.869Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9c119089-0446-47e1-9b33-c7edffb9a4f1","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
